# PRD: AGDF 0.20.0 Desktop release scope and honest qualification

Status: draft
Gate: PRD
Gate approval: open
Based on: UR
Date: 2026-10-22
Owner: AGDF maintainer
Traceability contract: criteria-chain-v1

## 1. Product Scope

Prepare one coherent AGDF 0.20.0 candidate for Codex Desktop and Claude Desktop as the intended release targets. Retain GitHub Copilot and OpenCode as experimental integrations with their adapters and regression coverage. Codex CLI on Linux and native Windows remains explicitly unqualified and is outside the mandatory 0.20.0 host matrix following the maintainer's explicit support-scope decision.

Record the maintainer's manual checks of both Desktop hosts, including normal AGDF invocation, upgrade and recovery, as reported passed. The answer "alle" confirms those named scenarios but supplies no concrete app version, model, candidate, session or primary capture. Codex Desktop OS is unspecified for this handcheck; Claude's other test computer was identified as Windows. Unknown fields remain unknown, and CLI tuples are never borrowed for Desktop.

Keep separate Windows Claude CLI evidence for its actual tuple/candidate after review and applicability validation. Existing five validator-accepted CLI cases for candidate 830d8b94 are not yet formal imported qualification. Earlier dirty macOS Codex CLI results remain diagnostic. Neither result qualifies Desktop, Linux or Windows Codex CLI.

Preparation, human-reported checks, candidate-bound qualification, human acceptance and publication are distinct outcomes. This revision permits closeout preparation with visible remaining obligations; it grants no release approval and does not waive candidate, ownership, failure, cleanup or approval safeguards.

| Host / surface | 0.20.0 scope | Available observation | Qualification boundary |
|---|---|---|---|
| Codex Desktop | Mandatory Desktop release target | Maintainer reports invocation, upgrade and recovery passed | Exact environment/candidate and demonstrated capability scope remain unverified |
| Claude Desktop | Mandatory Desktop release target; Windows test computer | Same three reported manual passes | Desktop coding/access path and exact environment/candidate remain unverified; no borrowed CLI identity |
| Claude CLI on Windows | Separate retained evidence, outside the mandatory Desktop matrix | Five validator-accepted cases for candidate 830d8b94 | Review/import and final-candidate applicability required for any qualified CLI claim |
| Codex CLI on macOS | Diagnostic evidence only | Five local diagnostic cases on earlier dirty candidate | No final-candidate or other-platform qualification |
| Codex CLI on Windows / Linux | Unqualified; outside mandatory matrix | No accepted native qualification | No supported or qualified claim inferred from Desktop or CI |
| GitHub Copilot / OpenCode | Experimental | Existing adapters and fixtures retained | No native 0.20.0 qualification claimed |

## 2. UX Intent And Success

- ui_ux_impact: low
- ux_intent_definition: Direct low-impact support and evidence labels from the current BROWNFIELD_REVIEW.md; no requested preview or new interaction.
- primary_user_intent: Identify whether the integration and actual host combination have merely been checked manually or qualified for the prepared candidate, then choose the appropriate next action.
- success_signal: Guidance and reports distinguish intended target, reported manual pass, qualified, pending/unverified, failed, diagnostic, unqualified and experimental without implying unsupported operating systems or capabilities.
- primary_decision_or_action: The maintainer assesses the exact evidence and remaining obligations before any human acceptance or separate release decision; installing users see the demonstrated scope.

## 3. Working Modes And Effective State

| working_mode | effective_state | visible_state_types | effective_state_authority | primary_state_presentation_owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Release preparation | Version/package coherence can pass before qualification | prepared; preparation_failed | Canonical version and package checks | Release readiness report |
| Desktop handcheck documentation | Original maintainer observations are retained with unknown fields | reported_manual_pass; identity_unverified | Attributed human report; no machine qualification inferred | Desktop handcheck record and compatibility/readiness report |
| Candidate-bound qualification | Each required Desktop combination/capability is supported or open | pending; failed; qualified | Reviewed native observations matching candidate and actual environment | Existing compatibility/readiness report |
| Separate CLI evidence | Observations apply only to their actual tuple/candidate and assurance | validated_pending_review; qualified; diagnostic | Existing native evidence validation and review | Evidence handoff and compatibility/readiness report |
| Unqualified/experimental path | Codex CLI Windows/Linux unqualified; Copilot/OpenCode experimental | unqualified; experimental | Explicit approved scope; no fixture or Desktop inference | Installation guidance and compatibility report |

These are meanings for existing outputs, not another persistent status machine, approval authority or acceptance register.

## 4. Activation, Blockers, Recovery And Transitions

- activation_and_deactivation: Use deliberate existing installation, consent and removal paths. Do not replace an active profile, transfer credentials or infer permission from an observation or successful MCP call.
- blockers_and_visible_next_actions: Missing identity or required capability proof leaves the corresponding qualification unverified. Recover original evidence first; if unavailable, name the exact missing fact and justify only targeted fresh verification. Wrong candidate, failed case or invalid ownership produces a concrete rejection and owner action.
- recovery_paths: Preserve original reports/results. Repair the affected prerequisite through its existing owner and retry the affected scope visibly. Candidate changes require applicable evidence reassessment. No blanket repetition of all handchecks is required solely because they were reported manually.
- relevant_state_transitions: Recording a human report changes documentation only. Reviewed matching observations may close their exact cases; unrelated OS/surface states stay unchanged. Missing/failed evidence blocks overall qualified/release-ready status. Scope revision removes old CLI rows from mandatory eligibility only after approved, tested policy migration, never by marking them passed. Publication remains separate.

## 5. Acceptance Criteria

### AC-001 — Coherent 0.20.0 candidate

criterion_id: AC-001

All canonical and derived release versions and exact dependent package requirements consistently identify 0.20.0. Canonical release preparation, package integrity, packaging and affected regression checks pass without weakening version/history or payload checks. Preparation publishes no package and creates no release tag.

### AC-002 — Accurate surface and support labels

criterion_id: AC-002

Public guidance, release notes, compatibility output and readiness reports consistently identify Codex Desktop and Claude Desktop as the intended targets and disclose observation method and limits. Codex CLI Windows/Linux stays explicitly unqualified and outside the mandatory 0.20.0 matrix. Copilot/OpenCode remain experimental with adapters/tests retained. Separate Claude Windows CLI evidence and Codex macOS diagnostics are labelled only within their demonstrated scope.

- working_mode: Desktop handcheck documentation, candidate-bound qualification and unqualified/experimental path.
- source_state: Existing policy/reporting still describes the old mandatory CLI matrix.
- trigger_action: Read installation, compatibility or candidate readiness guidance.
- expected_effective_state: Target intent, human-reported checks and reviewed qualification stay distinguishable.
- visible_feedback: Host, surface, OS where known, method, result and qualification limits are shown.
- blocker_failure_behavior: Unknown identity, missing or conflicting evidence cannot display qualified.
- recovery_next_action: Recover the specific original evidence or perform justified targeted verification.
- observable_success: A reader can identify the demonstrated scope and next action without inferring OS/surface support.
- required_evidence: Source/generated guidance consistency and report inspection, including unknown/manual states.

### AC-003 — Exact identity and assurance remain binding

criterion_id: AC-003

Every accepted qualified observation identifies the exact tested candidate, AGDF version, clean source commit and/or equivalent verified payload digests, actual host surface/version, OS, architecture, and model/Node where applicable. Unknown and genuinely inapplicable fields must remain distinct. Candidate and actual loaded identity must match; version prose, dirty diagnostics, generic chat, fixtures and human assertions without binding do not establish qualification. Preserve immutable provenance, review, containment and duplicate/mismatch rejection. Existing strict Codex CLI tuple/clean-commit safeguards remain for any retained optional CLI qualification path.

Incomplete manual reports may be retained as reported observations with explicit limits; they must not pass the qualified-record validator or silently acquire machine assurance.

### AC-004 — Codex Desktop evidence and unqualified CLI platforms

criterion_id: AC-004

Document the maintainer's Codex Desktop invocation, upgrade and recovery handchecks as reported passed, with missing identity and captures explicit. The mandatory Codex target is Desktop only. Qualification requires reviewed, candidate-bound native evidence demonstrating the claimed usable AGDF access path, deliberate installation, discovery, actual non-authorizing invocation, controlled invalid input, applicable skill continuation and cleanup. Demonstrate upgrade/recovery under the shared criterion. Neither Desktop evidence nor ordinary Windows/Linux CI qualifies Codex CLI on Windows/Linux; those paths stay unqualified outside mandatory release eligibility. Retain optional probes and ordinary platform regression coverage without invented passes or deleted failure history. Successful MCP alone proves no hook trust/execution or embedded MCP App rendering.

### AC-005 — Claude Desktop and separate Windows CLI evidence

criterion_id: AC-005

Document Claude Desktop's three named manual scenarios as reported passed on the other Windows test computer, without substituting CLI identity. Desktop qualification requires a fresh, identifiable Claude Code coding/access session with the actual loaded candidate and demonstrated AGDF path, plus the same installation/discovery, non-authorizing invocation, controlled failure, applicable skill and cleanup obligations as the Codex target. Generic Desktop chat and CLI calls do not substitute for this evidence.

Retain the five separately validator-accepted Windows Claude CLI cases (dispatch, invalid input, skill continuation, upgrade, recovery) for candidate 830d8b94 and their actual frozen tuple. Review/import and check applicability before any qualified CLI claim. Do not rerun successful cases without a concrete applicability gap; do not require local Claude credentials or execution on the preparation computer. CLI evidence remains separate and does not satisfy a mandatory Desktop row.

### AC-006 — Upgrade, bounded recovery and cleanup

criterion_id: AC-006

For each mandatory Desktop target, retain the human-reported upgrade/recovery result while separately assessing candidate-bound proof of upgrade from released 0.14.5 to final 0.20.0 and bounded recovery from a representative supported interrupted/stale/incomplete installation. Record starting identity, action, fresh effective loaded candidate, actual result and cleanup. Preserve project governance, unrelated settings and approval authority. Reuse existing supported mechanisms; no destructive migration, broad cache cleanup, unknown-ownership exception or weakened postcondition is permitted. If original handchecks do not supply these facts, keep only those facts unverified and identify a bounded evidence action.

### AC-007 — Mandatory matrix through existing release acceptance

criterion_id: AC-007

The single existing release eligibility path must enforce the approved Desktop matrix and reject absent, failed, stale, mixed-candidate, duplicate, incomplete or mismatched qualified evidence before publication. Migrate the former mandatory Linux/Windows Codex CLI dependency explicitly through canonical support policy and its consumers; never treat unexecuted CLI rows as passed. Preserve strict candidate, provenance, containment, ownership, cleanup, unknown-state and approval checks and the entire ordinary CI inventory/current timeouts. A documented handcheck is not a publication authorization or validator pass. Missing Desktop identity keeps qualification and publication eligibility open. Use the existing validators, imports and reports, not a second decision authority.

### AC-008 — Reviewable closeout preparation with visible limits

criterion_id: AC-008

Deliver coherent release notes, candidate/evidence instructions and a readiness report showing actual completed checks, exact references, human-reported scenarios, qualified tuples/capabilities, unknown Desktop facts, unqualified/experimental paths, retained diagnostics, failures and next actions. Refresh derived compatibility evidence through its owner. Preserve original redacted provenance, distinguish repository tests/CI/native observations/human acceptance, and expose every remaining mandatory obligation. Closeout preparation may be complete while qualification is pending; it must not imply clean release-ready completion, human acceptance or publication.

- working_mode: Release preparation, Desktop handcheck documentation and separate CLI evidence.
- source_state: Reported manual passes exist; original Desktop identity and final candidate applicability remain unverified.
- trigger_action: Record a report, review returned evidence or prepare closeout.
- expected_effective_state: Only validated applicable evidence changes its qualification result; human reporting remains separately attributed.
- visible_feedback: Completed and open obligations, known environment, unknown facts and one concrete next action per gap.
- blocker_failure_behavior: Missing/failed required proof prevents overall qualified/release-ready status.
- recovery_next_action: Recover original facts first or justify affected-case verification for the final candidate.
- observable_success: The maintainer can assess the next permitted step without guessing whether qualification, acceptance or publication occurred.
- required_evidence: Candidate report, preserved source statements, validated references and negative report/acceptance checks.

## 6. Non-Goals

Publication, tags, marketplace submission, active-profile replacement, credential transfer, qualification of Codex CLI Windows/Linux, Copilot/OpenCode native qualification, removal of experimental adapters, split release versions, new product/UI features, governance authority changes, fabricated host identity, assurance escalation or weakened safety/checks. No blanket retesting solely to replace documented manual assertions.

## 7. Users And Roles

- AGDF maintainer: Owns requested host scope, original manual assertions and human release/acceptance decisions.
- Native test executor: Preserves original observations, actual candidate/environment and bounded cleanup; identifies remaining concrete facts without assuming remote access.
- Evidence reviewer: Checks primary evidence, candidate/tuple/case applicability and immutable import, granting no gate approval.
- Installing users: Receive accurate Desktop scope and explicit unqualified/experimental/diagnostic limits.

## 8. Constraints

Retain approved UR, exact unchanged upstream approval and one version line. Use existing canonical metadata/schema/generation, installer/runtime, evidence, release and reporting owners. Current policy remains effective until renewed sources are approved and implemented. Renewed TP and required preparation precede implementation; retain code/tests for assessment. Preserve foreign worktree content. Respect host consent and separate technical permission from governance approval. Use a clean finalized candidate for release-grade proof. Preserve every ordinary CI test, present timeout, ownership and unknown-state safeguard. No requested interactive preview exists.

## 9. Evidence Requirements

The direct human source is DESKTOP_HANDCHECKS_20261022.md: both Desktop hosts and invocation/upgrade/recovery reported passed; concrete Desktop tuple, candidate/session and primary captures not supplied. Claude Windows is earlier test-computer context, not a CLI-to-Desktop identity transfer. Recording date is not execution date.

Retain the source-revision apply receipt and reviewed matrix provenance, canonical preparation/packaging results, applicable regression outcomes and independently reviewed native references. Preserve CLI candidate/tuple and review/import status and older diagnostic failures. Candidate-bound qualification needs observed expected/actual results, loaded identity, consent boundaries, cleanup and timestamps. Missing facts stay visible; no machine JSON/log/screenshot is manufactured from conversation assertions. No secrets, complete auth files, unrelated transcripts or credentials belong in returned evidence. No fresh host run or new CI result is claimed by authoring this PRD.

## 10. Risks And Open Questions

Concrete Desktop app/model/session/candidate and primary references are still unknown. Recover original evidence where available; if not recoverable, qualification remains bounded/unverified and only justified targeted verification follows. Final candidate changes require applicability assessment of existing Claude CLI evidence. Published 0.14.5 and development MCP capabilities differ, so upgrade proof must identify the effective new runtime. The canonical hostSupport schema, native records, publication graph and report consumers still encode the former matrix; design and test their coherent migration before changing eligibility. These are later design/execution obligations under the acceptance above, not hidden permission to waive product acceptance.

## Approval Decisions

| Decision | Timing | Status | Resolution | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Version and mandatory release targets | before_prd | resolved | Maintainer requested one 0.20.0 Desktop matrix for Codex and Claude; confirmed the reviewed PRD-source revision with "Revision anwenden" | AGDF maintainer |
| Unavailable and experimental paths | before_prd | resolved | Codex CLI Windows/Linux remains unqualified outside mandatory scope; Copilot/OpenCode remain experimental with adapters and tests retained | AGDF maintainer |
| Meaning of Desktop confirmation | before_prd | resolved | Record "alle" as all three named scenarios on both Desktop hosts; concrete versions/model/candidate were not supplied and remain unknown | AGDF maintainer |
| Qualification and release acceptance | before_prd | resolved | Preserve approved UR exact-candidate and no-false-qualification obligations; reports may be documented with limits, but missing mandatory proof blocks overall qualification and publication eligibility | AGDF maintainer |
| Upgrade and recovery obligations | before_prd | resolved | Retain 0.14.5 to final 0.20.0 upgrade, bounded supported recovery and preservation/cleanup safeguards; original report and verified substeps remain distinct | AGDF maintainer |
| Policy, record and report migration | later_sd | open | Extend existing metadata/schema/generator, evidence and publication/report owners; keep incomplete reports non-qualifying and prevent a parallel authority | Solution Design author |
| Original identity recovery and final candidate applicability | later_tp | open | Map each missing fact/case to original evidence recovery or justified targeted verification; review existing Windows CLI evidence before import/claim | Task/Test Plan author and evidence reviewer |

## 11. Next Step

Record and present this new PRD against exact retained UR and current Brownfield Review, then obtain a new deliberate Approval: PRD. That decision adopts the revised matrix and criteria and permits SD drafting only. Old PRD/SD/TP approvals do not carry forward; revision confirmation itself approves no gate, implementation or release.

## AGDF Approval Summary (de; source=en)

- Ziel: AGDF 0.20.0 für die tatsächlich geprüften Desktop-Hosts vorbereiten und den Abschluss mit belastbaren, ehrlichen Nachweisen vorbereiten.
- Umfang: Codex Desktop und Claude Desktop sind die Pflichtziele. Die Handprüfungen für normalen AGDF-Aufruf, Upgrade und Wiederherstellung sind als bestanden gemeldet. Konkrete Desktop-Versionen, Modelle und Kandidaten bleiben unbekannt. Claude-CLI-Windows-Belege bleiben separat; ältere Codex-macOS-CLI-Tests bleiben Diagnose.
- AC-001: Versionen, Abhängigkeiten und Pakete konsistent auf 0.20.0 vorbereiten und prüfen; nichts veröffentlichen oder taggen.
- AC-002: Desktop-Ziele und Beobachtungsmethode klar ausweisen; Codex CLI unter Windows/Linux bleibt unqualifiziert, Copilot/OpenCode bleiben experimentell mit ihren Adaptern und Tests.
- AC-003: Qualifikation verlangt exakte Kandidaten- und Umgebungsbindung. Unvollständige Handberichte werden erhalten, aber weder ergänzt noch als maschinell qualifiziert behandelt.
- AC-004: Codex-Desktop-Handprüfungen dokumentieren und beanspruchte Fähigkeiten am Kandidaten belegen; CLI- oder CI-Ergebnisse qualifizieren keine anderen Systeme oder Oberflächen.
- AC-005: Claude Desktop getrennt belegen; fünf vorhandene Windows-CLI-Fälle nur für ihre tatsächliche Identität und nach Prüfung/Import verwenden. Keine lokalen Claude-Zugangsdaten verlangen.
- AC-006: Upgrade von 0.14.5 und begrenzte Wiederherstellung mit tatsächlicher neuer Laufzeit, Erhalt fremder Einstellungen und sauberem Abschluss belegen; unbekannte Einzelnachweise bleiben offen.
- AC-007: Die bestehende Release-Prüfung konsistent auf die Desktop-Pflichtmatrix umstellen. Kandidaten-, Sicherheits-, Eigentums-, Fehler-, Freigabeprüfungen sowie alle normalen CI-Tests und Zeitlimits bleiben erhalten.
- AC-008: Abschlussunterlagen zeigen erledigte Prüfungen, menschliche Aussagen, Grenzen und offene Pflichtnachweise. Abschlussvorbereitung bedeutet noch keine Release-Bereitschaft oder menschliche Abnahme.
- Entscheidungen: Die Host-Auswahl und der Umfang der gemeldeten Handprüfungen stehen fest. Ursprüngliche Identitätsbelege zuerst wiederverwenden; nur begründete gezielte Nachprüfung. Fehlende Desktop-Bindung blockiert weiterhin Gesamtqualifikation und Veröffentlichung. Nach neuer PRD-Freigabe folgen erneuerte SD und TP; UR bleibt gültig.
